    "id": "neuro-action-potential-trace",
    "title": "Action Potential Trace",
    "field": "Neuroscience",
    "plotType": "Membrane-voltage-vs-time trace with characteristic spike shape",
    "description": "An action-potential trace plots the membrane voltage of a single neuron over milliseconds as it fires, capturing the canonical spike shape: a slow rise to threshold, a rapid depolarizing upstroke, repolarization, and an after-hyperpolarization dip below rest. Each phase corresponds to a specific ion-channel event, so the trace is essentially a readout of channel dynamics. Electrophysiologists use it to characterize cell type, excitability, and the effects of drugs on channels.",
